&lt;p&gt;Okta is seeking a highly proficient GEO Content Specialist to execute content-focused Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) strategies for Okta and Auth0. This is a mid-level individual contributor role focused on ensuring content is optimized for visibility and retrieval in the evolving landscape of AI Search/GEO/AEO. The ideal candidate is a reliable self-starter with a strong understanding of content, SEO, and the mechanisms of Large Language Models (LLMs).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Responsibilities &amp;amp; Execution:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Content Optimization:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute the strategy for structuring and optimizing content to promote content retrievability by LLMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and refine content blocks to be machine-parsable and aligned with semantic density and emerging AI answer formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand how content must be structured (&lt;a href=&quot;http://schema.org&quot;&gt;schema.org&lt;/a&gt; and JSON-LD) for LLM visibility and apply best practices while adhering to brand and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities by reviewing GEO prompt data, analyzing competitors, and thinking creatively about content needs for the business.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GEO Knowledge &amp;amp; Application:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a working knowledge of how LLMs function, relevant KPIs, and content-related GEO best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply concepts such as vector embeddings, RAG, grounding, chunks, passages, and citations in daily content work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on industry changes related to GEO/AEO/AIO and the future of organic visibility.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data &amp;amp; Workflow:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize a data-driven approach to execute content tasks and identify content performance trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with &lt;strong&gt;Customer First&lt;/strong&gt; teams to ensure optimized content is published effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage assigned content tasks effectively, meeting deadlines and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI in content analysis, editing and production workstreams to improve efficiency and output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze SEO and GEO key performance metrics for Customer First subdomains, providing insights and recommendations to stakeholders for optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional experience in SEO, and content strategy, with a focus on content optimization and/or content development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands how content is rewarded in both LLMs and modern-day search ranking algorithms (this position is not about traditional SEO keyword optimization).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with current GEO concepts and the role of LLMs in search.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of multiple SEO platforms such as STAT, SEMRush, Lumar/DeepCrawl, Looker Studio, Google Analytics, Google Search Console, Screaming Frog, Profound, and similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in data analysis and insights gathering for content output and performance tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, with the ability to articulate content requirements and results clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using HTML, Salesforce Experience Builder,&amp;nbsp; or similar enterprise-level systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in the post-Sales roles and Identity and Access Management (IAM), B2B marketing, SAAS, or the cybersecurity domain is preferred, but not required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
