&lt;p&gt;The Role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a driven, curious, and empathetic product management leader to push the envelope of Okta’s market footprint by growing our integration ecosystem. As Director of Product Management for Okta integration ecosystem, you will be responsible for product strategy, and managing a PM team dedicated to evolving the Okta built integrations across all the product lines. This is a high-impact role, and if you’re passionate about improving customer security and engaging with a vibrant community, we’re looking for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work Location: Bengaluru, Karnataka, India&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work Mode: Hybrid (2-3 days Onsite per week)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy and growth of Okta’s build integrations through product vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect with key partners and customers to distill down feature asks and pain points into true requirements that deliver broad customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop roadmaps that make hard tradeoffs and prioritize the highest value work first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build compelling hypotheses and find ways to validate assumptions at low cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with global cross-functional teams, including engineering, ISVs, tech partnerships, and marketing, to ensure the successful launch and adoption of ISV experience enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with development scrum teams (PM, UX, Dev) to deliver valuable new integration targeted features and product improvements to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct research and analysis to identify integration needs, and use this information to inform strategic vision, innovation, product decisions, prioritization and roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and communicate product requirements, including features, user experience, and technical specifications, to engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage product data to continually get smarter about how to improve our existing products, and work across the business to drive adoption and success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track industry trends and think strategically to develop solutions that are differentiated from the competition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of technology product management, experience in enterprise scale SaaS products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or product managing the user experience of a partner joining, engaging, and building upon a core enterprise software platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, communication (presentation, verbal and written) and collaboration skills. You easily work with customers and colleagues across different functions and backgrounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of owning and delivering on large strategic projects - you can see the big picture, but deliver on the details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated business results from products, features or capabilities you have shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills. You can produce solid action plans from often incomplete, conflicting or ambiguous inputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for Okta’s huge opportunity and growth potential, and general thirst for learning with an ability to go broad and deep across business and technical contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with identity and access management (IAM) platforms and security products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across the product management lifecycle for enterprise products or services, partner considerations surfaced in the user experience in particular&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Identity and Access management protocols and products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS in Computer Science, Computer Engineering or equivalent experience that allows you to rationalize and influence technical design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in technical or business field, MBA helpful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P12154_3477804&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;At Okta, we are on a mission to free everyone to safely use any technology. As the &lt;strong&gt;Director of Product Management – Platform&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own and drive the multi-year product strategy for Okta’s foundational platform suite. Reporting directly to the Chief Product Officer, this role has complete product ownership over the core infrastructure powering Okta’s enterprise identity engine.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will manage and mentor a team of &lt;strong&gt;Product Managers&lt;/strong&gt;, translating Okta’s overarching company vision into an execution-focused roadmap. Your platform portfolio spans identity automation (&lt;strong&gt;Okta Workflows&lt;/strong&gt;), core cloud identity directory (&lt;strong&gt;Universal Directory&lt;/strong&gt;), multi-org governance (&lt;strong&gt;Okta Aerial&lt;/strong&gt;), business continuity (&lt;strong&gt;Backup &amp;amp; Recovery&lt;/strong&gt;), administrative design standards (&lt;strong&gt;UI Platform&lt;/strong&gt;), monetization primitives (&lt;strong&gt;Licensing &amp;amp; Metering&lt;/strong&gt;), and end-to-end &lt;strong&gt;Multi-Product Experiences&lt;/strong&gt; (including AI assistants, unified policy layer, universal search, admin dashboard, and platform RBAC).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Strategic Vision &amp;amp; Core Product Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate Okta&#39;s overarching enterprise vision into a comprehensive, multi-year product strategy and roadmap for the entire Platform portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage a deep understanding of competitive market dynamics, security architecture trends, and SaaS infrastructure evolutions to anticipate market shifts and maintain Okta&#39;s competitive advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the CPO, CTO, architectural leadership, and cross-functional execs to align platform investments with broader corporate strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Execution, Business Impact &amp;amp; Operational Allocation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Take direct accountability for core business results, high-throughput platform feature launches, and global platform resilience/uptime SLAs.&lt;br&gt;• Arbitrate and mediate complex cross-team resource allocations, balancing architectural scaling and technical debt against customer-facing multi-product initiatives.&lt;br&gt;• Drive cross-product convergence across seven key product pillars:&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-Product Experiences:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead cross-product convergence including the &lt;strong&gt;Unified Policy Layer&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;AI Assistants&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Universal Search&lt;/strong&gt;, centralized &lt;strong&gt;Admin Dashboard&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Platform RBAC for Admins&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Okta Workflows:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive low-code/no-code orchestration, event-driven execution, and integration ecosystem scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Universal Directory (UD):&lt;/strong&gt; Scale Okta’s central cloud identity store for massive global enterprise customer performance and reliability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Okta Aerial:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver Okta&#39;s centralized multi-org visibility, management, and governance platform.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UI Platform:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the common admin UI framework, design system, and frontend architecture across all Okta products.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Licensing &amp;amp; Metering:&lt;/strong&gt; Build global billing primitives, consumption tracking, feature flag architectures, and entitlement engines.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backup &amp;amp; Recovery:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure enterprise-grade disaster recovery, configuration backups, and point-in-time restore capabilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Managerial Leadership &amp;amp; Team Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, retain, and develop a high-performing team of Product Managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire aggressively to raise talent density across the product organization, fostering an environment of technical rigor, accountability, and customer empathy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act swiftly on performance gaps, actively coaching team members toward career growth while holding high execution standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Executive &amp;amp; Market Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary executive champion for Okta&#39;s platform strategy with CISOs, CIOs, strategic enterprise accounts, and industry analysts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product Marketing, Sales, and Customer Success leadership to translate abstract platform capabilities into clear go-to-market value propositions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience (M5 Standards)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 9–13+ years of progressive Product Management experience in B2B enterprise SaaS, developer platforms, or core infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; 3+ years of direct people management experience managing product managers (including experience managing senior/principal PMs or Group PMs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain &amp;amp; Technical Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong architectural foundation in identity systems, administrative access control (RBAC), usage metering, or AI-assisted enterprise workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution Track Record:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience driving high-throughput launches and owning business/platform outcomes across interconnected product lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated success in mediating complex engineering resource trade-offs and cross-product dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional strategic narrative development, board-level communication, and executive presence with internal and external enterprise stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or higher in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior leadership experience across workflow orchestration engines, governance platforms, or disaster recovery solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct domain knowledge in Identity and Access Management (IAM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Okta Leadership Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raises Talent Density:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively hires, coaches, and retains top-tier PM talent to elevate team capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Love Our Customers:&lt;/strong&gt; Focuses platform outcomes on making life easier, safer, and more productive for enterprise admins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Balances immediate execution demands against a multi-year vision for enterprise-scale platform cohesion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drives Results:&lt;/strong&gt; Takes end-to-end accountability for business impact, platform scaling, and product delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;br&gt;#LI-MM&lt;br&gt;P6583_3512040&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual base salary range for this position for candidates located in the San Francisco Bay area is between:  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$258,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$355,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Below is the annual base salary range for candidates located in California (excluding San Francisco Bay Area), Colorado, Illinois, New York and Washington. Your actual base salary will depend on factors such as your skills, qualifications, experience, and work location. In addition, Okta offers equity (where applicable), bonus, and benefits, including health, dental and vision insurance, 401(k), flexible spending account, and paid leave (including PTO and parental leave) in accordance with our applicable plans and policies. To learn more about our Total Rewards program please visit: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://rewards.okta.com/us&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;https://rewards.okta.com/us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual base salary range for this position for candidates located in California (excluding San Francisco Bay Area), Colorado, Illinois, New York, and Washington is between:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$316,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Based in Tokyo, we are seeking a Director to lead our high-growth Japan Sales Development team.&amp;nbsp;As the leader of Sales Development, you will be responsible for owning the management of overall inbound&amp;nbsp;business development and outbound prospecting pipeline strategy and execution. You will lead &amp;amp;&amp;nbsp;motivate a team of highly driven SDRs and implement efficient processes &amp;amp; tools that optimize for scale&amp;nbsp;in a fast-paced innovative and collaborative environment. This role reports to the Senior Director, Sales&amp;nbsp;Development (APJ).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;This is a high visibility role that is responsible for hiring, on-boarding, and coaching a group of high&amp;nbsp;performing sales professionals while collaborating with many other departments within our Go To&amp;nbsp;Market Function (Marketing, Operations and Sales etc.). You will own Japan xDR Go to Market strategy,&amp;nbsp;with a goal of improving the existing teams productivity, efficiency and outbound quality to build and&amp;nbsp;progress pipeline to revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;At Okta, our mission is to maintain a people-first, diverse, and inclusive culture. You will be responsible&amp;nbsp;for building the Japan xDR team culture with a focus on coaching and mentoring. You will need to be an&amp;nbsp;expert in prospecting and account planning strategies with a high growth company and must be able to&amp;nbsp;educate others effectively in these areas. You will also focus on enabling continued growth of their reps&amp;nbsp;in preparation for their progression here at Okta. If you thrive in a fast-paced environment and are eager&amp;nbsp;to take ownership over a large revenue generating piece of the business, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Core Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Leadership &amp;amp; Business Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end strategy for Sales Development across Japan, setting the sales&amp;nbsp;vision, operating model, and key performance metrics that fuel regional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish operational rigor and a culture of high performance across the SDR&amp;nbsp;organization, ensuring the team is aligned to the go-to-market strategy and consistently&lt;br&gt;produces high-quality pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate market trends, customer insights, and competitive intelligence into targeted&amp;nbsp;prospecting strategies that elevate pipeline performance across segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional collaboration with Sales, Marketing, Channel, and RevOps to&amp;nbsp;ensure alignment on account coverage, persona focus, inbound/outbound prioritization,&lt;br&gt;and the SDR → AE handoff model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outbound Excellence &amp;amp; Leading by Example&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and lead the execution of a robust outbound strategy that systematically&amp;nbsp;generates high-quality new business pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model exceptional outbound behaviors by actively participating in call blitzes,&amp;nbsp;demonstrating best-in-class outreach techniques, objection handling, and call&amp;nbsp;preparation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and reinforce high standards for outbound quality, personalization, and&amp;nbsp;consistency—ensuring the team understands what “great” looks like.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage tools, AI, intent data, and industry insights to create advanced outbound plays,&amp;nbsp;win-back motions, event-triggered outreach, and persona-based engagement strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect outbound performance regularly, identifying root causes of gaps and driving&amp;nbsp;rapid corrective actions across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence &amp;amp; Execution Discipline&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure tools, systems, and processes (e.g., Outreach, CRM, data enrichment, AI tools)&amp;nbsp;are optimized to support efficient prospecting and high conversion outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular inspections of operational workflows, prospecting motions, and&amp;nbsp;productivity metrics, driving continuous improvement and operational innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement governance frameworks to uphold SDR productivity, quality, compliance, and&amp;nbsp;forecasting accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable mechanisms for pipeline generation, including playbooks, sequences,&amp;nbsp;cadences, discovery frameworks, and qualification standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with RevOps to build capacity models, coverage plans, and forecasting processes&amp;nbsp;based on ramp profiles and inbound supply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Development &amp;amp; Frontline Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, coach, and inspire a high-performing SDR leadership bench, creating strong second-line leaders capable of developing their teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement structured coaching frameworks that elevate SDR skills in prospecting,&amp;nbsp;qualifying, discovery, and opportunity creation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide targeted, actionable feedback supported by regular call reviews, performance&amp;nbsp;inspections, and structured development plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop career pathways that enable rapid ramp, strong performance, and optimized&amp;nbsp;tenure, while promoting internal mobility into AE and other GTM roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive a culture of accountability, transparency, and continuous improvement—ensuring&amp;nbsp;underperformance is addressed quickly and equitably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster an inclusive, engaged, and collaborative team environment where individuals feel&amp;nbsp;supported, challenged, and motivated to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership &amp;amp; Stakeholder Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Marketing to ensure inbound demand, scoring, routing, and&amp;nbsp;follow-up SLAs are aligned and optimized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Sales Leaders to continuously refine territory models, target personas,&amp;nbsp;and qualification standards to maximize coverage and opportunity quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work jointly with Enablement to design onboarding, ramping programs, skills&amp;nbsp;development sessions, and ongoing coaching tracks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the voice of the SDR organization at the leadership table, ensuring the team’s&amp;nbsp;insights inform regional planning and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline Growth &amp;amp; Business Outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive execution of the Sales Development strategy to ensure pipeline targets are&amp;nbsp;consistently met or exceeded.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the team to create high-quality, well-qualified opportunities that accelerate sales&amp;nbsp;cycles and improve win rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, analyze, and report on SDR performance, conversion rates, and pipeline&amp;nbsp;health—delivering actionable insights and areas of improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously refine the pipeline generation strategy to adapt to changing market&amp;nbsp;conditions and business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10–15+ years in Sales Development, Inside Sales, or GTM People Manager roles.&amp;nbsp;Including leading managers (second-line leadership).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building and scaling SDR teams and delivering consistent, high-quality&amp;nbsp;pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success driving outbound strategy, messaging, ICP refinement, and&amp;nbsp;persona-based plays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of partnering with Sales, Marketing, RevOps, and Enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with forecasting, capacity planning, segmentation, and SDR/Sales handoff&amp;nbsp;models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Capabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operator with deep experience in sales tools (Salesforce, Outreach, AI tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven decision maker with strong analytical and diagnostic skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design and optimize prospecting workflows, playbooks, coaching frameworks,&amp;nbsp;and qualification standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in building scalable programs for onboarding, coaching, and talent development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication in English &amp;amp; Japanese, executive presence,&amp;nbsp;and influence skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Behavioral Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads from the front—models high-quality outbound calls, outreach, preparation, and&amp;nbsp;objection handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coach who develops both SDRs and frontline managers through structured&amp;nbsp;frameworks and regular feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creates a culture of accountability, collaboration, and high performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operates with integrity, transparency, and a strong sense of ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable driving both strategic planning and hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adhere to the 4-day RTO policy (and potential future shift to 5 days RTO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in SaaS, cybersecurity, or enterprise software environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Marketing, or a related field (or equivalent experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Okta’s Top 5 Core Leadership Competencies are part of the deeply ingrained principles that guide all of&amp;nbsp;our company’s actions. They also align strongly to our cultural cornerstones, our Okta values: love our&amp;nbsp;customers, empower our people, never stop innovating, act with integrity, and maintain transparency.&lt;br&gt;It’s our expectation that our managers and leaders embody these core competencies:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds Effective Teams: Building strong-identity teams that apply their diverse skills and&amp;nbsp;perspectives to achieve common goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates Self-Awareness (EQ): Using a combination of feedback and reflection to gain&amp;nbsp;productive insight into personal strengths and weaknesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develops Talent: Developing people to meet both their career goals and the organization’s goals.&lt;/li&gt;
