&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the briefing strategy for our flagship San Francisco center, measuring success and regularly reporting out ROI and pipeline impact to executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Briefing Execution: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead high-touch briefing engagements from initial request to post-briefing follow-up, ensuring an exceptional, white-glove experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM &amp;amp; Account Team Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with Enterprise Sales, Customer Success, and Solutions Engineers to define briefing objectives, customize agendas, build prep materials, and facilitate pre-briefing alignment and post-brief ing debriefs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Speaker Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Source, prep, and manage internal discussion leaders (VP+ and C-Suite); continuously cultivate and enable a network of top-tier internal speakers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations &amp;amp; Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain post-briefing tracking and metrics in Salesforce (or briefing management tools) to measure opportunity influence and deal acceleration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics &amp;amp; Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with Workplace and AV/IT teams to ensure seamless center operations and flawless day-of delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years in Go-To-Market roles (Enterprise Sales, Customer Success, Solutions Consulting, Field Marketing) and/or running high-stakes Executive Briefing Centers for enterprise tech/SaaS companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Presence:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record of consulting with and advising VPs and C-Suite executives (both internal and customer-facing).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Business Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of complex B2B sales cycles and how tailored briefing content moves accounts from evaluation to closed-won.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Tooling Skills: Experience using briefing management platforms and core enterprise toolstacks— hands-on experience with BriefingSource, Google Drive, Salesforce, and Tableau is a strong plus.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; High-agency, detail-oriented self-starter who thrives in fast-paced environments, anticipates risks before they happen, and delivers white-glove service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Flawless written and verbal communication skills with a knack for distilling complex topics into compelling executive narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel &amp;amp; Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Based in San Francisco with a minimum of 2 days/week in the office (up to 25% travel required, including international).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
