&lt;h4&gt;Position Description:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Research Operations Program Manager at Okta, you will play a crucial role in building and enabling an impactful beta program. Via close collaboration across research, design, product, engineering teams, QA, and release teams, you will programmatically manage cross-functional teams’ research needs. You will proactively build and manage the operations for a beta program, collaborating with other cross functional functions to plan the necessary infrastructure for this programming to be successful, following compliance and governance best practices.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;In this role, you’ll get to:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead research operations and panel management for beta programming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively across multiple teams to empower Okta staff to carry out impactful research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help manage the general pipeline of inbound research requests from various teams across the organization, including prioritizing new and ongoing projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain research documentation, templates and other informational resources for research methods, procedures and techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop internal activities that help cultivate Okta’s broader user research culture and community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help teams access relevant knowledge through reviews of past research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cross-functional team members to analyze, share, and store their findings and insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow your colleagues’ research skills and competencies through training workshops, presentations and documentation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct primary research with both Okta staff and potentially customers to inform the improvement of user research operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that user research programs and processes meet accessibility standards and promote inclusion among both Okta staff and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with ethical research standards as well as privacy policies and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the continuing improvement of our research systems, such as our participant panel and research repository&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and maintain a database of existing and prospective research participants, proactively building out our panel of participants as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership in program management methodologies and best practices, ensuring consistent and successful delivery of projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and manage potential risks, develop mitigation strategies, and resolve project challenges proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Qualities that would make you a great candidate for this role:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience working in design, product or research operations roles&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A holistic and collaborative approach to solving problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive approach to making research a team sport&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong sense of ownership, transparency, flexibility, and ability to self-initiate projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or managing beta and/or early release evaluation programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with QA and Release teams to ship product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing customer panels and/or participant communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of best practices for leveraging AI tooling, such as Claude and Gemini, to improve efficiency and streamline processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the practices and impacts of inclusive research and design approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and multitasking skills to manage multiple programs simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinking and the ability to align multiple functions with organizational goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration abilities, with experience engaging with both technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of UX research approaches and methodologies (including direct research experience to ensure quality of research)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management and/or operational expertise to ensure programs are sustainable, scalable and delivered within constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity and possess a desire to overcome obstacles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A curious mind, a quick learner with a bias for action, and an attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to train/coach others to ensure the program runs successfully and the people who you’re guiding to execute research themselves are fully supported&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Education&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master’s degree in psychology, human-computer interaction, program management, business (or other related field) or equivalent work experience&lt;/p&gt;
