&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Senior Strategic Alliance Manager, Indian GSIs opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Sr. Strategic Alliance Manager - Indian SIs you will play a critical role in building and expanding our relationships with large Indian Global System Integrators (GSIs). This is a strategic position that requires a blend of leadership, technical acumen and business insight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement partnership strategies with a named group of Indian GSIs to grow their Okta practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with regional sales leaders globally to drive initiatives and foster collaborative relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the annual partnership planning process, including joint investments, target customers, pipeline and execution plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a regular rhythm of business and executive interlocks to ensure alignment and mutual success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and outline key areas of opportunity and growth within the partnership framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin as an individual contributor with a focus on building the foundation for these strategic alliances, and be able to quickly scale to manage a team, providing leadership and understanding the nuances of global-to-local dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring to the&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;role &amp;amp; what we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 8+ years of experience in building alliances with Global Systems Integrators (co-marketing, investment strategies, practice creation, product/solution development).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep and recent experience working within the Indian GSI landscape. You MUST have existing relationships with entities including but not limited to: Wipro, TCS, Infosys, and HCL.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in strategic alliance management, preferably in the security sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and technical knowledge relevant to identity and access management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage and negotiate at the executive level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to set strategy, plan effectively, and drive execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel as needed to meet with partners and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Marketing, Technology, or a related field. An advanced degree is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
