&lt;h2 data-local-id=&quot;85b8117a34e6&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;heading&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The Emerging Products Design Team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;f244368879b1&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Emerging Products is an org pillar inside Auth0. We figure out what&#39;s next. You&#39;ll be designing systems that help developers secure AI agents, manage granular permissions, and build on identity primitives that don&#39;t fully exist yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;2fc814d396b0&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Engineers, PMs, and Designers work on the same problems at the same time. There is no design-then-build sequence. There&#39;s just build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-local-id=&quot;0ed94ed2f216&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;heading&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;cea9821bc0d2&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;When everyone on the team can generate UI, the designer&#39;s role shifts. You become the person responsible for strong systems thinking, taste, quality, experience, and being the voice of the customer. You hold the quality bar when speed is pushing everything toward &quot;fine.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ak-ul&quot; data-local-id=&quot;c863b4f5-9a57-4196-98fb-1496a7a6596f&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;bulletList&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;f1b389c5-c60c-409e-a7e8-448776013956&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;listItem&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;c64b38d8284b&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Prototype at volume&lt;/strong&gt;: Use AI tools and code to explore dozens of directions fast, then narrow based on what works and what solves the actual problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;939f2cb0-143a-4e75-bda8-05c442de129b&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;listItem&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;9951c6fd8b8a&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Design in the codebase: &lt;/strong&gt;Work within our React and Next.js environment to refine components and interactions where users will actually experience them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;5da906a6-8e5b-4d9d-a6cf-420df5cf8ded&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;listItem&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;d7307c4706a7&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Simplify complexity:&lt;/strong&gt; Turn authorization models, SDK patterns, and security flows into interfaces that feel clear without losing precision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;cef289c7-1250-4800-bdee-5b289a5a8035&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;listItem&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;5d164012ba31&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Raise the craft:&lt;/strong&gt; Help the broader design org see what this way of working looks like in practice. We&#39;re all figuring this out together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-local-id=&quot;e4ff11e1b17f&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;heading&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What you’ll bring to the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ak-ul&quot; data-local-id=&quot;3bac17c7-a00e-4aab-bd47-3da888d72836&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;bulletList&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;62e72888-df3d-4a40-a768-b9d4a77553f5&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;listItem&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;0b636959a727&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;You have craft:&lt;/strong&gt; This matters most. Considered typography, intentional spacing, polished micro-interactions, details that show someone genuinely cared. We&#39;re looking for someone with a refined sense of design taste/aesthetics and a deep appreciation for the details that create a polished user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;fe8b91c4-85d7-415b-9df0-3210cd8fd6b3&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;listItem&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;a7464771a04d&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;You build:&lt;/strong&gt; 6+ years of design experience, but somewhere along the way you started prototyping in the browser, shipping side projects, or writing production code because you wanted the interaction exactly right.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;95dc4b1d-603f-40cd-9336-ea8062f8b2ea&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;listItem&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;8c811e65edf6&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;You have a real AI practice:&lt;/strong&gt; Not experimentation, but an actual workflow. You have opinions about where AI tools help and where they fall short.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;a613057b-bfd0-491d-b5d9-36ead1966e08&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;listItem&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;e2ab23115b5e&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;You design for developers:&lt;/strong&gt; Tools, APIs, CLIs, SDKs, and admin dashboards. You know &quot;simple&quot; means something different for this audience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-local-id=&quot;691f387617c3&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;heading&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Note for when applying&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;224fe7346526&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;In your application, please include a link to your portfolio with password (if protected). We prioritize a review of your design craft and any examples of your work in code.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Below is the annual base salary range for candidates located in San Francisco Bay Area. Your actual base salary will depend on factors such as your skills, qualifications, experience, and work location. In addition, Okta offers equity (where applicable), bonus, and benefits, including health, dental and vision insurance, 401(k), flexible spending account, and paid leave (including PTO and parental leave) in accordance with our applicable plans and policies. To learn more about our Total Rewards program please visit:&lt;a href=&quot;https://rewards.okta.com/us&quot;&gt; https://rewards.okta.com/us&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt; The annual base salary range for this position for candidates located in the San Francisco Bay area is between: &lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$193,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Designer — AX &amp;amp; Growth (DLG)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Auth0, part of Okta, is redefining identity for a world where users aren&#39;t only human. AI agents are beginning to sign up, authenticate, and act autonomously — and Auth0 is building the infrastructure and experience layer for that shift. This role is a foundational design hire on&amp;nbsp; Auth0&#39;s India Design Team, part of the global design team. Working at the frontier of&amp;nbsp; Agent Experience (AX) : designing for a largely headless, invisible-UI world where the &quot;user&quot; is often code acting with intent, not a person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join a small pod of PMs and engineers actively defining Auth0&#39;s agentic vision from scratch — there&#39;s no existing pattern library, so you&#39;ll help create it: how agents sign up, authenticate, execute tasks, and how humans stay in control without micromanaging them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alongside this, you&#39;ll own signup and onboarding design for a new customer: the&amp;nbsp; AI-powered developer, whose workflows involve agents and automated tooling from day one. The same instincts that build trust for a human overseeing an agent also build trust for a developer signing up for a self-serve product. We&#39;re looking for a&amp;nbsp; self-starter&amp;nbsp; who generates their own hypotheses and builds the roadmap as they go.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent Experience (AX)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Shape Auth0&#39;s agentic vision alongside a small, fast-moving team of PMs and engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Define the &quot;what&quot; for agents — interaction models for signup, execution, and backend operations, largely invisible to a screen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Define the &quot;how&quot; for humans — trust, transparency, and control (errors, edge cases, audit trails) for orchestrating agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Identify the problems worth solving yourself; establish patterns and protocols others adopt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Own the full lifecycle: definition, prototyping, validation, iteration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Growth &amp;amp; Onboarding (DLG)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Define signup and onboarding for the AI-powered developer — rethinking self-service as workflows become increasingly automated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Own subscription, pricing &amp;amp; packaging strategy end to end; shape the Growth roadmap with Product and Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Define how design impact is measured (e.g., via Pendo, Heap); lead research and turn insight into action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Simplify high-leverage developer workflows into elegant, self-service experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Craft &amp;amp; Influence&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Be a thought partner to the design manager; raise the craft bar across the Global Design Team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Mentor designers; translate AI/technical concepts into practical guidance for PMs and engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Represent design in roadmap discussions for both AX and Growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- 10+ years of human-centered product design experience with a portfolio showing strategic ownership and strong craft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- A true self-starter — you&#39;ve built experiences or practices from scratch, without a roadmap handed to you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Comfortable designing for headless, low-UI, API-first surfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-&amp;nbsp; Experience designing for AI agents or agentic systems is a huge plus&amp;nbsp; — you&#39;ve tackled invisible-UI, trust, or automation problems before, not just discussed them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Track record owning onboarding/self-service experiences at scale, backed by PLG and conversion metrics fluency (Pendo, Heap, or similar).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Comfortable in ambiguity, technical conversations, and fast-moving, undefined team settings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- A multiplier — you elevate others and build alignment without formal authority.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Bonus: engineering/front-end background.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Help write the vision, not just implement it — a founding voice on AX and Growth&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Shape two frontiers at once: invisible AX for agents, and growth for AI-powered developers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Operate at staff scope, with real influence over strategy and craft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- We believe in augmentation, not replacement — and in design as problem-solving, not artifacts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Be a founder of a new discipline, architecting how growth and agentic systems work together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;L1-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P23063_3156978&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Okta is looking for a talented Staff Product Designer (you!) who shares our passion for bringing simple, yet powerful product experiences to our enterprise admins. At Okta,&amp;nbsp; we&#39;re building a world where anyone can safely use any technology, and we&#39;re specifically focused on protecting the future of work. We bring simple and secure access to people and organizations everywhere, promising to not only protect the identities of our customers&#39; workforce and users, but to ask, “what more can we make possible?”&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Which is where you come in! ​​As a Staff Product Designer for Okta, you’ll work with a globally distributed design team to apply your craft and expertise on a range of products and services. Our culture provides the opportunity to explore the technologies we’re researching and investing in. Some of your work will be functional, practical user experience design, where you will help our design team drive cohesive user experience across Okta’s portfolio of products. Other work will be speculative, generative explorations that you carry out in collaboration and partnership across the organization to flesh out, frame, and help prioritize solutions in an ever-evolving and complex, often ambiguous, problem space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finer print&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead user experience strategy and execution for our Okta Research &amp;amp; Development (ORD) business unit. Specifically, ORD will solve every identity use case at work – for all types of people (employees, business partners, contractors, frontline workers), for all types of resources (SaaS, servers, privileged resources, machines, etc.), for the largest and most secure businesses in the world. As a designer, your focus will be on helping us build a secure, trusted, and unified platform with deep integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a holistic, human-centered approach to design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide and oversee the UX strategy alongside cross-functional partners, collaborating to take products from concept to launch and define the long term strategy for your product area.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and facilitate co-creation design workshops with Product Management, Engineering and Design to define opportunities within our products to solve valuable customer problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft user-centered artifacts and end-to-end journeys to align teams contributing to Workforce Identity Management around the broader user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other Okta designers to ensure consistency across interface experiences across different user scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire teams to think bigger and act smaller, instilling an iterative process and fail forward mentality to design simple and delightful user interfaces for new and existing Okta products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate, mentor, and educate on the benefits of design thinking to product teams and new designers alike; partnering with UX team members to uphold our principles and standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior designers and contribute toward team-level and design practice and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Design Leadership to define and drive the frameworks, contracts, and standards for others to be able to then build on top of and add value to, ensuring the quality of UX delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find creative ways to continuously learn from customers and users; collaborating with user researchers to research and synthesize user needs to help conceive, define, test and evolve solutions for our users across a range of mediums and experiences; Advocate for users and delivering user and customer outcomes in a dynamic work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help product designers create success metrics to illustrate a clear understanding how their designs impact customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present work, concepts, and new ideas to cross-functional team members, adjacent teams, and senior leadership; working to distill complex technical problems into clear, conceptual models and simple, elegant solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep abreast of competitor products and industry trends; Perform competitive and comparative analysis to understand existing patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate and encourage thoughtful use of AI for brainstorming and iterating on potential solutions, prototyping, and collaborating with team member.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience leading cross-discipline teams and exemplify leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious and have experience incorporating AI into your design process, including the ability to craft tools, iterate on ideas collaboratively with AI, and document sophisticated prompts for scaled use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate AI-generated outputs for technical accuracy, design system adherence, and ease of use to serve as a necessary quality bar before designs move to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are passionate about solving complex problems, crafting and sharing product and design UX principles to help teams deliver cohesive user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are great at collaborating, You share work early and often, and seek constructive feedback from peers and stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have the heart of a teacher and can help mentor and train people. You build and share empathy with people in order to deeply understand them and their needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a thought leader, undertaking explorations into new technologies and territories while also delivering practical designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are someone who sees design as a partner in shaping strategic and operational product and UX outcome; comfortable owning all stages of design for multiple teams within a given product area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring a systems-thinking lens to the conversation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are passionate about supporting teams with a wide variety of experience, backgrounds, and interests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your portfolio will show that you&#39;ve worked on complex and/or technical projects across all aspects of the design process (conceptual design, interaction design, information architecture, and visual design)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant work experience as a Product Designer or UX Designer, with a portfolio showcasing shipped B2B or enterprise products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in a related field or relevant work experience as a Product Designer or UX Designer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Figma, Sketch, Adobe Creative Suite, and / or similar design tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possesses at least a basic understanding of HTML / CSS / JavaScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can provide a digital portfolio that showcases solid skills across a variety of projects, including work that has been seen and used successfully in actual products. (Portfolio link required when applying.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-MM&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;br&gt;P25192_3445285&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Below is the annual salary range for candidates located in Canada. Your actual salary will depend on factors such as your skills, qualifications, and experience. In addition, Okta offers equity (where applicable), bonus, and benefits, including health, dental, and vision insurance, RRSP with a match, healthcare spending, telemedicine, and paid leave (including PTO and parental leave) in accordance with our applicable plans and policies. To learn more about our Total Rewards program, please visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://rewards.okta.com/can&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://rewards.okta.com/can&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1705181614985000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw29oi6BOXve4rhySFpzzvao&quot;&gt;https://rewards.okta.com/can&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual base salary range for this position for candidates located in Canada is between:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$193,000 CAD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Okta Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://rewards.okta.com&quot;&gt;Supporting Your Well-Being&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/okta-for-good/&quot;&gt;Driving Social Impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.okta.com/company/talent-connection-community/&quot;&gt;Developing Talent and Fostering Connection + Community&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are intentional about connection. Our global community, spanning over 20 offices worldwide, is united by a drive to innovate. Your journey begins with an immersive, in-person onboarding experience designed to accelerate your impact and connect you to our mission and team from day one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Okta is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, marital status, age, physical or mental disability, or status as a protected veteran. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and convictions records, consistent with applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If reasonable accommodation is needed to complete any part of the job application, interview process, or onboarding please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1EfiEYZrIyhA2X4Fijk0R3RKYOzNoS3wtvyM4nhbZnXE/edit&quot;&gt;use this Form&lt;/a&gt; to request an accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notice for New York City Applicants &amp;amp; Employees: Okta may use Automated Employment Decision Tools (AEDT), as defined by New York City Local Law 144, that use artificial intelligence, machine learning, or other automated processes to assist in our recruitment and hiring process. In accordance with NYC Local Law 144, if you are an applicant or employee residing in New York City, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://talent.okta.com/new-york-city-aedt-notice.html&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; to view our full NYC AEDT Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Every Identity, from AI to Human&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Identity is the key to unlocking the potential of AI. Okta secures AI by building the trusted, neutral infrastructure that enables organizations to safely embrace this new era. This work requires a relentless drive to solve complex challenges with real-world stakes. We are looking for builders and owners who operate with speed and urgency and execute with excellence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an opportunity to do career-defining work. We&#39;re all in on this mission. If you are too, let&#39;s talk.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The Team&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Login and MFA team owns the most consequential surface in software: the exact moment someone proves who they are.&amp;nbsp;Getting this right means designing security that&#39;s invisible when it works, flows that guide without friction, and experiences that people trust without thinking twice. We&#39;re looking for a designer who obsesses over the details that make that possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join a distributed and diverse team of designers who see design as both craft and catalyst. We believe design is never static, it evolves with our users, our products, and our own curiosity. Some days that means diving deep into research and validation, others it&#39;s refining existing flows, and often it&#39;s imagining bold new ways to move our product forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team thrives on collaboration and feedback. We learn from one another, challenge ourselves to raise the bar, and create space to experiment and grow. Designers here have real ownership, influencing product direction alongside engineering and product management while shaping experiences that reach millions of people worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re energized by complex problems, motivated to push boundaries, and eager to hone your craft while making a lasting impact, this is the place to do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The Role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Designer, you&#39;ll tackle some of the hardest design challenges in identity: making authentication seamless for end users while remaining powerful and configurable for the developers who build on it. You&#39;ll lead design across Auth0&#39;s key login and multi factor authentication flows by guiding strategy and raising the craft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When everyone on the team can generate UI, the designer&#39;s role shifts. You become the person responsible for strong systems thinking, taste, quality, experience, and being the voice of the customer. You hold the quality bar when speed is pushing everything toward &quot;fine.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prototype at volume:&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI tools and code to explore dozens of directions fast, then narrow based on what works and what solves the actual problem. The artifacts you create will be functional and inclusive of all Auth0 developer interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simplify complexity:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape intuitive, scalable experiences for our customers with high standards for security and composability. You&#39;ll be designing customization journeys that make secure and frictionless authentication seamless.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the craft:&lt;/strong&gt; Help the broader design org see what this way of working looks like in practice. We&#39;re all figuring this out together. You&#39;ll take pride in expanding your contributions through code and research-driven insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you&#39;ll bring to the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have craft:&lt;/strong&gt; This matters most. Considered typography, intentional spacing, polished micro-interactions, details that show someone genuinely cared. We&#39;re looking for someone with a refined sense of design taste and a deep appreciation for the details that create a polished, trustworthy experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You build:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve established a mature AI workflow that helps you bring ideas to life quickly. Instead of letting the backlog of small design debt collect, you take action and fix things directly in code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have a real AI practice:&lt;/strong&gt; Not experimentation, but an actual workflow. You have opinions about where AI tools help and where they fall short.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You simplify:&lt;/strong&gt; Auth0 is a robust and composable product. It is your job to create clarity and moments of magic amidst the complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Note for when applying&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your application, please include a link to your portfolio with password (if protected). We prioritize a review of your design craft and any examples of your work in code.&lt;/p&gt;
