&lt;h3&gt;Staff Product Marketing Manager, Privileged Access Management&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Get to know Okta&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Okta is The World’s Identity Company. We free everyone to safely use any technology, anywhere, on any device or app. Our flexible and neutral products, Okta Platform and Auth0 Platform, provide secure access, authentication, and automation, placing identity at the core of business security and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Okta, we celebrate a variety of perspectives and experiences. We are not looking for someone who checks every single box - we’re looking for lifelong learners and people who can make us better with their unique experiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our team! We’re building a world where identity belongs to you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Staff Product Marketing Manager to join our team and lead go-to-market strategy, positioning, and adoption for Okta Privileged Access. This is a strategic, high-impact role for a seasoned PMM who thrives at the intersection of product, customer, strategy, and marketing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will be able to take complex security concepts and turn them into compelling stories for a variety of audiences and personas. They will need to balance diverse inputs from stakeholders, market insights, competitive trends and customer needs to formulate a crystal clear POV that can translate into differentiated positioning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale the PAM transformation narrative:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to Okta&#39;s strategic narrative for privileged access by crafting compelling positioning that moves the market from seeing PAM as a legacy security checkbox to seeing it as a modern, cloud-native enabler of Zero Trust&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create differentiated messaging:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop frameworks, slides, press releases, and other high-impact deliverables that articulate the product&#39;s value proposition for sales, customers, and analysts&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive inbound product marketing:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as a critical partner to Product Management by connecting market opportunities to roadmap decisions. Use market insights and competitive analysis to influence and shape the future direction of Okta Privileged Access&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver strategic market insights:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish a framework for analyzing PAM market trends, competitive dynamics, and customer friction points, ensuring actionable insights are delivered back to product and GTM teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Orchestrate high-impact launches:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead GTM execution for PAM features and products, ensuring cross-functional alignment and that every launch delivers on strategic growth goals&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish the blueprint for success:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify how leading organizations use Okta Privileged Access to modernize their security posture and distill these success stories into repeatable blueprints that help prospects realize full value from the platform&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with marketing:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure the PAM narrative is integrated into campaigns and demand generation programs, enabling the field to target the right buyers and influencers effectively&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you’ll bring to the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years experience as a product marketer in cybersecurity or identity management, preferably in the PAM space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of marketing to a highly technical audience. You must be comfortable working with and marketing to technical buyers within enterprises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of creating product and/or solutions-specific messaging and content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management skills, can manage multiple priorities in a dynamic environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership skills, with the ability to influence stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to drive programs from initiation to success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting customer interviews and being the “voice of the customer”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
